rse":3,"text":"A fire devours before them, and behind them, a flame burns. The land is as the garden of Eden before them, and behind them, a desolate wilderness. Yes, and no one has escaped them."},{"verse":4,"text":"Their appearance is as the appearance of horses, and they run as horsemen."},{"verse":5,"text":"Like the noise of chariots on the tops of the mountains, they leap, like the noise of a flame of fire that devours the stubble, like a strong people set in battle array."},{"verse":6,"text":"At their presence the peoples are in anguish. All faces have grown pale."},{"verse":7,"text":"They run like mighty men. They climb the wall like warriors. They each march in his line, and they don’t swerve off course."},{"verse":8,"text":"One doesn’t jostle another. They each march in their own path. They burst through the defenses and don’t break ranks."},{"verse":9,"text":"They rush on the city. They run on the wall. They climb up into the houses. They enter in at the windows like thieves."},{"verse":10,"text":"The earth quakes before them. The heavens tremble. The sun and the moon are darkened, and the stars withdraw their shining."},{"verse":11,"text":"The LORD thunders his voice before his army, for his forces are very great; for he is strong who obeys his command; for the day of the LORD is great and very awesome, and who can endure it?"},{"verse":12,"text":"“Yet even now,” says the LORD, “turn to me with all your heart, and with fasting, and with weeping, and with mourning.”"},{"verse":13,"text":"Tear your heart and not your garments, and turn to the LORD, your God; for he is gracious and merciful, slow to anger, and abundant in loving kindness, and relents from sending calamity."},{"verse":14,"text":"Who knows? He may turn and relent, and leave a blessing behind him, even a meal offering and a drink offering to the LORD, your God."},{"verse":15,"text":"Blow the trumpet in Zion! Sanctify a fast. Call a solemn assembly."},{"verse":16,"text":"Gather the people. Sanctify the assembly. Assemble the elders. Gather the children, and those who nurse from breasts. Let the bridegroom go out of his room, and the bride out of her chamber."},{"verse":17,"text":"Let the priests, the ministers of the LORD, weep between the porch and the altar, and let them say, “Spare your people, LORD, and don’t give your heritage to reproach, that the nations should rule over them. Why should they say among the peoples, ‘Where is their God?’”"},{"verse":18,"text":"Then the LORD was jealous for his land, and had pity on his people."},{"verse":19,"text":"The LORD answered his people, “Behold, I will send you grain, new wine, and oil, and you will be satisfied with them; and I will no more make you a reproach among the nations."},{"verse":20,"text":"But I will remove the northern army far away from you, and will drive it into a barren and desolate land, its front into the eastern sea, and its back into the western sea; and its stench will come up, and its bad smell will rise.” Surely he has done great things."},{"verse":21,"text":"Land, don’t be afraid. Be glad and rejoice, for the LORD has done great things."},{"verse":22,"text":"Don’t be afraid, you animals of the field; for the pastures of the wilderness spring up, for the tree bears its fruit. The fig tree and the vine yield their strength."},{"verse":23,"text":"“Be glad then, you children of Zion, and rejoice in the LORD, your God; for he gives you the early rain in just measure, and he causes the rain to come down for you, the early rain and the latter rain, as before."},{"verse":24,"text":"The threshing floors will be full of wheat, and the vats will overflow with new wine and oil."},{"verse":25,"text":"I will restore to you the years that the swarming locust has eaten, the great locust, the grasshopper, and the caterpillar, my great army, which I sent among you."},{"verse":26,"text":"You will have plenty to eat and be satisfied, and will praise the name of the LORD, your God, who has dealt wondrously with you; and my people will never again be disappointed."},{"verse":27,"text":"You will know that I am among Israel, and that I am the LORD, your God, and there is no one else; and my people will never again be disappointed."},{"verse":28,"text":"“It will happen afterward, that I will pour out my Spirit on all flesh; and your sons and your daughters will prophesy. Your old men will dream dreams. Your young men will see visions."},{"verse":29,"text":"And also on the servants and on the handmaids in those days, I will pour out my Spirit."},{"verse":30,"text":"I will show wonders in the heavens and on the earth: blood, fire, and pillars of smoke."},{"verse":31,"text":"The sun will be turned into darkness, and the moon into blood, before the great and terrible day of the LORD comes."},{"verse":32,"text":"It will happen that whoever will call on the LORD’s name shall be saved; for in Mount Zion and in Jerusalem there will be those who escape, as the LORD has said, and among the remnant, those whom the LORD calls."}],"hasArtwork":true,"artworkUrl":"/data/images/books/joel.svg","availableLangs":["zh-CN"]},{"id":"joel_3","bookSlug":"joel","chapter":3,"reference":"Joel 3","title":"Joel 3 — Public Domain Study","topics":["joel","joel","ot","scripture","約珥書","约珥书","上帝要審判萬民","神要审判万民"],"snippet":{"zh-CN":"「到那日，我使犹大和耶路撒冷被掳之人归回的时候，"},"tokens":{"21":2,"29":1,"joel":9,"public":2,"domain":2,"study":1,"ot":1,"scripture":1,"約珥書":1,"约珥书":2,"上帝要審判萬民":1,"神要审判万民":1,"到那日":2,"我使犹大和耶路撒冷被掳之人归回的时候":1,"我要聚集万民":1,"带他们下到约沙法谷":1,"在那里施行审判":1,"因为他们将我的百姓":1,"就是我的产业以色列":1,"分散在列国中":1,"又分取我的地土":1,"且为我的百姓拈阄":1,"将童子换妓女":1,"卖童女买酒喝":1,"泰尔":2,"西顿":2,"和非利士四境的人哪":1,"你们与我何干":1,"你们要报复我吗":1,"若报复我":1,"我必使报应速速归到你们的头上":1,"你们既然夺取我的金银":1,"又将我可爱的宝物带入你们宫殿":1,"并将犹大人和耶路撒冷人卖给希腊人":1,"使他们远离自己的境界":1,"我必激动他们离开你们所卖到之地":1,"又必使报应归到你们的头上":1,"我必将你们的儿女卖在犹大人的手中":1,"他们必卖给远方示巴国的人":1,"这是耶和华说的":1,"当在万民中宣告说":1,"要预备打仗":1,"激动勇士":1,"使一切战士上前来":1,"要将犁头打成刀剑":1,"将镰刀打成戈矛":1,"软弱的要说":1,"我有勇力":1,"四围的列国啊":1,"你们要速速地来":1,"一同聚集":1,"耶和华啊":1,"求你使你的大能者降临